// title: List Automatically Closed Incidents · Sentinel
// date: 2026-10-21
// product: Sentinel
// tables: SecurityIncident
// purpose: List the incidents that are automatically closed by Microsoft Defender XDR. It is good practice to get an overview of the automatically closed incidents and review them once every x period to determine if all the risks have been covered. The amount of automatically closed incidents depend on the Aut
// source: https://github.com/Bert-JanP/Hunting-Queries-Detection-Rules/blob/65d11700e1cb878403d87312acdd6b9a8dd622c1/Security%20Operations/XDRAutomaticallyClosedIncidents.md
// kind: repo
// author: Bert-Jan Pals
// license: BSD-3-Clause (as stated by the repository)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
SecurityIncident
| where ProviderName == "Microsoft 365 Defender" and ModifiedBy == "Microsoft 365 Defender"
| extend OwnerObjectID = tostring(Owner.objectId)
| where Status == "Closed" and Classification == "Undetermined"
| where isempty(OwnerObjectID)
| where isnotempty(ClassificationComment)
